   "html_text": "The logico-grammatical context that characterized twelfth-century discussions gave rise to a set of specific issues. The problem of the substantiality of the signification exhibited by proper names such as ‘Socrates’ became a major preoccupation in logic, where ‘Socrates’ had to belong to the category of substance by the essential determination through which it signifies the subject and not only because what it signifies is indeed a substance. But this was the case in grammar as well. In Priscia",
